---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Device from "../../components/Device.astro";
import { projects } from "../../projects";

const twain = projects.find((p) => p.slug === "twain")!;
const shots = [
  { src: "/media/twain-conversation.webp", alt: "Face to face: each half reads the conversation in its own language", w: 600, h: 1298 },
  { src: "/media/twain-thread.webp", alt: "The thread layout in light mode: the whole conversation, both languages", w: 600, h: 1298 },
  { src: "/media/twain-languages.webp", alt: "Choosing a language: search, the current pair, native names", w: 600, h: 1298 },
];
---

<Base
  title="Twain — a face-to-face live translator · Pavle Dujkic"
  description="Put the phone on the table and talk: each person reads and hears the other in their own language, about as soon as they stop speaking."
  image="og-twain.png"
>
  <link slot="head" rel="preload" as="image" href={`/${twain.clip!.poster}`} fetchpriority="high" />

  <article class="case">
    <header class="head wrap">
      <a class="back" href="/#work"><span aria-hidden="true">← </span>Work</a>
      <p class="label">Case study · {twain.year} · {twain.platforms}</p>
      <h1 class="serif">{twain.title}</h1>
      <p class="tagline">{twain.tagline}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="stage wrap">
      <Device project={twain} size="hero" />
    </div>

    <div class="body wrap">
      <section>
        <h2 class="serif">The idea</h2>
        <p>
          Put the phone on the table between two people and talk. Each of you reads and hears the other in your own
          language. One half of the screen faces you; the other is turned around for the person across the table, so
          nobody has to pass the phone back and forth.
        </p>
        <p>
          Twain runs on Alibaba’s <code>qwen3.8-livetranslate-flash-realtime</code>, a model that listens and translates
          in one step: 60 languages in, 29 spoken out. Serbian, which the model can’t target, comes out as Bosnian text
          read by the phone’s own voice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="serif">Fast where it counts</h2>
        <p>
          A conversation is only as good as its pauses. Twain keeps a translation session warm for each direction before
          anyone touches the screen, plus a spare connection that turns a language change into a quarter-second message
          instead of a reconnect. Audio leaves the phone in 50&nbsp;ms pieces, and the model closes each phrase after
          0.6&nbsp;s of silence, so the translation is usually complete before the speaker’s turn has even ended.
        </p>
        <dl class="figures">
          <div><dt>0.76 s</dt><dd>last word → complete translation</dd></div>
          <div><dt>0.90 s</dt><dd>last word → translated voice (the turn-end pause)</dd></div>
          <div><dt>2 ms</dt><dd>end of a turn → voice starts</dd></div>
          <div><dt>0.25 s</dt><dd>to change a language</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="note">Medians from repeated live conversations against the real model. About $0.002 per turn with voice.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="serif">Made for noisy places</h2>
        <p>
          Loud cafés broke the first version: a detector that listened for loudness opened the mic on background chatter
          and never let it close. Twain now listens for the pitch of a voice against a noise floor it learns from the room,
          and switches on the phone’s own noise suppression and echo cancellation. Across 78 noisy recordings it gets 51
          turns right where the old detector got 6, and noise alone never opens the mic. Where it’s really loud, you can
          hold your half while you talk.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="serif">Tested against the real thing</h2>
        <p>
          Every change runs against the live model, not just a mock: the engine with recorded voices, the app in a
          browser, native builds on an Android emulator and an iPhone simulator, and a performance suite that replays
          conversations under café, street and fan noise.
        </p>
        <p>
          That’s how the model’s strangest habit turned up. After a noisy moment it sometimes answers clear speech with
          nothing, then quietly merges those words into a later turn. Twain now notices an empty answer to speech it
          clearly heard and sends the turn again on a fresh connection, about 1.7&nbsp;s later.
        </p>
        <table>
          <caption class="visually-hidden">Before and after resending empty answers</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Before</th><th scope="col">After</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Noisy turns translated</th><td>14 of 39</td><td>34 of 39</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Clean turns lost</th><td>2 of 14</td><td>0 of 33</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="serif">The small things</h2>
        <ul class="small-things">
          <li>Auto-turn hands the mic to the other person once the translation has played.</li>
          <li>Your own words appear as you speak, so you can see you’re being heard.</li>
          <li>“Again” replays the last translation; one tap on the centre stops everything.</li>
          <li>The other person is greeted in their own language before anyone speaks.</li>
          <li>Haptics on every turn change, dark and light, VoiceOver and TalkBack.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="gallery wrap" role="list">
      {
        shots.map((s) => (
          <figure role="listitem">
            <img src={s.src} alt={s.alt} width={s.w} height={s.h} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </figure>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="body wrap">
      <section>
        <h2 class="label">Built with</h2>
        <ul class="chips">{twain.stack.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .head {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .back:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .head h1 {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(4rem, 13vw, 8.5rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .tagline {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2vw, 1.375rem);
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  .stage {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem);
  }

  .body {
    max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--gutter));
  }

  section + section {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .body h2.serif {
    font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .body p + p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .body p,
  .body li {
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  code {
    font: 0.85em/1 ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    padding: 0.15em 0.4em;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--text);
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  .figures {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem 2rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 1.75rem 0;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .figures dt {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--text);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .figures dd {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }

  .note {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  th,
  td {
    padding: 0.8rem 0;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  thead th {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }

  tbody th {
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  td:last-child {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 550;
  }

  .small-things {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .small-things li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.85rem 0 0.85rem 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .small-things li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.15rem;
    top: 1.45rem;
    width: 0.45rem;
    height: 0.45rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7a45, #3da9fc);
  }

  .gallery {
    display: grid;
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    grid-auto-columns: min(15rem, 62vw);
    gap: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    margin-block: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 6rem);
    overflow-x: auto;
    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
    scrollbar-width: none;
  }

  .gallery figure {
    margin: 0;
    scroll-snap-align: center;
  }

  .gallery img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 1.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    box-shadow: 0 1.5rem 3rem -1.5rem rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .gallery {
      grid-auto-flow: row;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 16rem));
      justify-content: center;
      overflow: visible;
    }
  }

  .chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .chips li {
    padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }
</style>
